A||||1||alpha||What should I be paying for steel?||||1||
Z||000000||alpha||12-14-2000||10:10 AM||||I am going to need to aquire about 50 ft of 1" X .083 wall box steel for a project I am working on. Does anyone havea  rough estimate of what that should cost? I would just like to have some idea before I go to and get it.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gonzo_442||12-14-2000||08:00 PM||||the depends on the lengths you need, the type of steel, and where you buy it.<P>if you need it all in one 50' piece it will cost quite a bit more than if you could use say, 5 10' pieces.<P>the types typically used in a form such as that are stainless (polished or not), carbon steel (and galvanized), or alloy 4130.<BR>of them, carbon is cheapest, then galvanized carbon, followed by stainless and alloy in that order. the difference is usually not that large, a couple of dollars per 10'. <P>among these options, you're looking at $1.50 to $10 a foot. if you're flexible with the size, you could get a better price.<BR>also, since you only said 1", this assumes a square (1"x1"x.083w).<P>ymmv <P>------------------<BR>--<BR>g||||reg||1
